<article class="env-lemma" id="077B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/077B">Lemma <span data-tag="077B">110.52.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $G$ be a group scheme over $S$. The stack $G\textit{-Principal}$ classifying principal homogeneous $G$-spaces (see Examples of Stacks, Subsection <a href="/tag/04UN" data-tag="04UN">95.14.5</a>) and the stack $G\textit{-Torsors}$ classifying fppf $G$-torsors (see Examples of Stacks, Subsection <a href="/tag/04UR" data-tag="04UR">95.14.8</a>) are not equivalent in general. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The discussion above shows that the functor $G\textit{-Torsors} \to G\textit{-Principal}$ isn't essentially surjective in general. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>